 ## Background
-The Sparse Voxel Octree (SVO) is a fundamental data structure in volume rendering and pathfinding [S1, unofficial]. The recursive dense builder approach [S1, unofficial] is often used in ray marching engines for its simplicity. The GPU-based level-by-level construction [S3, unofficial] is associated with modern voxelization pipelines for real-time rendering. The UE5 pathfinding variant [S2, unofficial] demonstrates the application of SVOs in game development for dynamic obstacle avoidance.
+The Sparse Voxel Octree (SVO) Builder is a method for constructing hierarchical acceleration structures for volume rendering and raycasting. The dense recursive build method is documented in unofficial GitHub repositories [S1, unofficial]. GPU-based iterative builds are also documented in unofficial GitHub repositories [S3, unofficial]. Pathfinding-specific SVO constructions are documented in unofficial video tutorials [S2, unofficial].
 
